&#x20;The export loop  Problem is solved now.&#x20;

&#x20;Have you implemented saving a project in the local folder?  If that's the case, shouldn't the homepage shows the list of  Internal projects instead of previously imported files?  Otherwise, how would the user open an internally saved project?&#x20;

&#x20;Also, when a file just opens or just gets restored, the icon will become the clock icon again and stay as the clock icon until I move the pointer.  This is not a big issue, so if it's complicated to fix, you don't have to fix it.

&#x20;I found another problem. when the agent responds to my question,  It seems that each word triggers an autosave.&#x20;

you can check debug\_Wed\_Sep\_30\_08\_44\_45\_86311.log.0 for what happened.&#x20;

&#x20;I suspect that I only discovered one of the many cases when the autosave would be triggered excessively.  Can we have a high level review about our architecture and see what we can do to eliminate this problem rather than dealing with it on a case-by-case basis.

